-- title:
--   Admissible bottom layer and level field at q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime subject to the hypothesis `hq2` that $q = 2$, and $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with `hqM'` asserting $q \nmid M'$. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and `hA` (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`) says that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. The field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` is the subfield of Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ generated by the Laurent expansions $j$ and $j_{M'}$; `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`; and `fieldBar q M'` is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the $X_H$ function field of level $q^2M'$, $H$ being the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. A finset $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$ is given, and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places, i.e. of the places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(j) \in \mathrm{ssJSet}$. The hypothesis `hle` gives the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   The datum $R_0$ is a constant reduction of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` relative to $A$: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the geometric level-$M'$ field, a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto the reduced field with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ and with scaling by constants, together with a map on places preserving degrees and carrying divisors of functions with nonvanishing residue to the order divisors of their residues. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Next, $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ (`hπ`) and $\pi \in A$ (`hπP`), and $\zeta$ is an element of `Idx q`, the set of primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, used to index the level automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Two families of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` are given: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$.
--
--   The Igusa hypotheses are: `hIg_inf`, which characterises $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ (for $\infty$ the point `lineInfty q` represented by $(1,0)$) as the set of $f$ for which there are Laurent series $x, y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f \cdot \bar y = \bar x$ in Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, where $\bar{\;}$ denotes coefficientwise inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$; `hIg`, which for each $\ell$ provides $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\mathrm{redQ}(q)(\gamma)\cdot\infty = \ell$ and $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, the injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, which says that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullbacks along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$.
--
--   The supersingular hypotheses are: `hSS_A`, that for each $s \in W$ and $x \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ the image of $x$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ precisely when $x \in A$; `hSS_over`, which for $s \in W$ and $f$ in `R₀.integers` subject to the condition that $f$ is regular at every place at which the element $\hat\jmath \in$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq`) is regular, and subject to the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lying in the valuation ring of the place $s$, asserts that the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and that for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of that image and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is its own pullback along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that for each $s \in W$ there is $t \in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that $t - a$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   The descent base consists of: a subfield $K_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ algebraic over $K_0$ and $\pi \in K_0$ (`hπK₀`); a henselian discrete valuation ring $A_0$ which is a domain, together with an injective local ring homomorphism $\iota : A_0 \to A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is exactly $A \cap K_0$ (`hιK₀`) and such that the composite of $\iota$ with the residue map of $A$ is surjective (`hres`); and a generator $\varpi_0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ (`hϖ₀`) with $\iota(\varpi_0) = \pi$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (`hϖ₀π`).
--
--   Finally, the coefficient field data: a subfield $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` characterised by `hF₀` as the set of $f$ all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$; the hypothesis `hjF₀` that the image of $\hat\jmath$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$; and an $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ with `hj₀` saying that the structure map sends $a$ to the image of $\iota(a)$ under $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exist an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that: the underlying set of $k_0$ is that of $K_0$; $\pi_0 = \pi$; the preimage $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring; its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$; it is a henselian local ring; its residue field is algebraically closed; every $a \in A$ admits $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ and $a - c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$; there exist a prime $\ell \geq 3$ with $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$ and an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; there is a unit $u$ of $A$ with $\pi_0^{q^2-1} = q\,u$; and there is a ring isomorphism $e : A_0 \simeq A \cap k_0$ with $e(a) = \iota(a)$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for all $a \in A_0$.
--
--   The conclusion continues with clauses about the bottom intermediate field $\bot$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$: an element $x$ of $\bot$ lies in the comap of $A$ along $\bot \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ if and only if $x \in A$; $\bot$ is finite-dimensional over $k_0$; the comap of $A$ along $\bot \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ is a discrete valuation ring and a henselian local ring; and there is a ring isomorphism $e_0 : A_0 \simeq A \cap \bot$ with $e_0(a) = \iota(a)$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for all $a \in A_0$.
--
--   The final clause concerns the level field, formed with respect to the $k_0$-algebra structure on `fieldBar q M'` obtained by composing $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`: there exists an intermediate field $F_0'$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ such that (i) $f \in F_0'$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ is of the form $c$ for some $c \in k_0$; (ii) the join of $F_0'$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the range of $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'` is everything; (iii) $F_0'$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; (iv) for every finite-dimensional intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in the join of $F_0'$ and the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, linear independence of $c$ over $K'$ together with $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$; (v) every $f$ whose Laurent series lies in the range of `coeffEmb` $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, i.e. has rational coefficients, belongs to $F_0'$; (vi) $F_0'$ and $F_0$ have the same elements; and (vii) there is a ring isomorphism $\Phi$ from $F_0$ onto the join of $F_0'$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\bot$, which preserves underlying elements of `fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case of the statement that the bottom layer of the tower over the descent base is admissible: it produces the base field $k_0$ with its tame element $\pi_0$, the full package of properties of $A \cap k_0$ (henselian discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $\pi_0$, algebraically closed residue field exhausting the residues of $A$, auxiliary root of unity, $\pi_0^{q^2-1} = q u$), the identification of $A_0$ with $A \cap k_0$ and with $A \cap \bot$, and the identification of the coefficient field $F_0$ with the level field $F_0'$ over $k_0$. It is obtained from the corresponding admissibility statement for small constants and from the construction of the level field over $k_0$, and is used by the subsequent analysis of the Igusa and Drinfeld charts over finite layers of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$.
